# T-998: Specificity-based instance resolution (type-system-health-s841-followup)
# Verifies that a user-defined multi-param type class with FD is accepted by
# the type checker.
#
# Specificity-based instance resolution (concrete > polymorphic) is a type-checker
# concern. When multiple instances match, the more specific one should win.
#
# NOTE: Runtime dispatch of user-defined class methods is not yet wired up.
# Instance registration and specificity-based selection are future milestones.
[
  # Define a two-param class with FD (a, b) → b
  # This class models addition where the result type is determined by the operand types.
  MyAddable: [class [let MyAddable a b]
    [determines: [[[a b] b]]]
    add: [Fn@b [a b]]]

  # Prove the class declaration was accepted: use prelude + for Int addition
  result: [+ 10 32]
]

---

%.result
=== out
Int(42)
